  "result": "I found the bug and wrote a fix plan. I haven't changed any code yet because plan mode is on, and I couldn't submit the plan for approval because the ExitPlanMode tool isn't available here.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py:603` splits the command line for completion. It uses Python's lower-level `shlex.shlex` splitter, which treats `#` as the start of a comment by default. So everything from a `#` onward is thrown away: `split_arg_string(\"cli a#b c\")` returns `[\"cli\", \"a\"]` instead of `[\"cli\", \"a#b\", \"c\"]`. The function's docstring says it splits \"as with `shlex.split`\", and `shlex.split` doesn't treat `#` as a comment by default.\n\n**Planned fix:**\n1. **The fix itself:** add `lex.commenters = \"\"` right after `lex.whitespace_split = True` in `split_arg_string`.\n2. **Tests in `tests/test_parser.py`:** add these cases to `test_split_arg_string`:\n   - `\"cli a#b c\"`\n   - `\"cli #b\"`\n   - `\"cli 'a#b\"` (an unclosed quote)\n3. **Test in `tests/test_shell_completion.py`:** add one end-to-end completion test with a `#` in an argument value.\n4. **Changelog:** add an unreleased `8.5.1` entry to `CHANGES.md`, since 8.5.0 has already been released.\n\n**How I'll check it:** run `pytest tests/test_parser.py tests/test_shell_completion.py`, then the full `pytest` suite.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\shell-completion-gives-wrong-abstract-papert.md`. Tell me to go ahead and I'll make the changes.",
